meta {
  name: Create a local test user
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{supabaseUrl}}/auth/v1/admin/users
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  apikey: {{serviceRoleKey}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{serviceRoleKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{testEmail}}",
    "password": "{{testPassword}}",
    "email_confirm": true
  }
}

docs {
  Not one of our endpoints: this talks to the local Supabase GoTrue admin API to
  mint a password user, because the real site only offers OAuth and magic links
  and neither is scriptable from a REST client.

  Needs `serviceRoleKey` set in the environment (`supabase status` prints it, or
  read SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY from the repo-root `.env`). That key bypasses
  all authorization, so it belongs only in the LOCAL environment.

  The user this creates has an `auth.users` row but no profile, so it starts at
  onboarding: run `Me profile and account / Create my profile` next.

  Local only. Against production this is both wrong and dangerous.
}
